      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition made molecularly targeted cancer therapy a compelling clinical reality and changed treatment of chronic myeloid leukemia.",
        "attribution": "Lydon, Druker, and Sawyers capture pivotal drug discovery, clinical translation, and mechanistic development.",
        "maturity": "The therapeutic principle has long been validated in CML and has influenced precision oncology more generally.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Attribution must distinguish the therapeutic-inhibition breakthrough from the earlier discovery of BCR-ABL itself."
        ]
